@startuml sequence-diagram-3

' Sheet 3/4 - A4 portrait. See sequence-diagram.puml for the whole diagram.
skinparam dpi 200
scale max 1500*2150

title node-sso-consumer - WSS authentication and realtime delivery of ME\nSheet 3/4: standing by and receiving the ME

autonumber 44

actor "User" as User

participant "Front Application\nBrowser" as Browser
participant "SSO Client\nnode-sso-consumer/client" as Client
participant "Node Application\nnode-sso-consumer" as App
participant "Realtime Bridge\nnode-sso-consumer" as Bridge
participant "x-core\nSSO / Realtime Provider" as XCore


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED FROM SHEET 2/4:
the WebSocket is open, the application and the user are authenticated,
the three topics are subscribed.
end note


group "Ticket valid" branch (continued)

    == 8. Standing by ==

    ... WSS connection open ...

    Client -> Bridge : ping
    Bridge -> XCore : ping
    XCore --> Bridge : pong
    Bridge --> Client : pong

    note over Client, XCore
    The ping only serves
    to check that the connection is alive.

    It is NOT a ME refresh.

    The ping ALWAYS goes out. It is the SILENCE CHECK that only
    acts while the tab is VISIBLE: a hidden tab has its timers
    throttled, so the check would read a silence that never
    happened and hang up a perfectly healthy socket.

    The answer carries the topic "#pong" and nothing else:
    it has already done its job by arriving.
    end note


    == 9. The account changes in x-core ==

    XCore -> XCore : Profile change\nOR permissions\nOR rights

    XCore -> XCore : Generates the new SsoMe


    == 10. ME sent straight over WebSocket ==

    XCore --> Bridge : WSS frame\nme-changed\n{ data: SsoMe }

    Bridge --> Client : WSS frame\nme-changed\n{ data: SsoMe }

    note over Bridge, Client
    HERE the ME really is
    carried over WebSocket Secure.
    end note

    Client -> Client : readMe(frame.data)

    alt The account no longer satisfies portail (subset of) global
        Client -> Client : ended()
        Client --> Browser : Session over, back to the portal

        note over Client, Browser
        Losing access to THIS application is not
        one right fewer, it is the door.

        The frame therefore means SIGN-OUT and not repaint:
        otherwise the reader sits on a page the server
        has already started refusing.
        end note

    else The account is still admitted
        Client -> Client : onAccount(me)
        Client --> Browser : New ME available
    end


    note over Browser, XCore
    The new ME was carried directly
    inside the WebSocket frame.

    NO refresh, NO polling, NO GET /me.

    One exception only, and it is not periodic:
    on a me-sessions frame, see sheet 4/4.
    end note

end


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED ON SHEET 4/4:
the other ways a session ends, and the reconnection.
end note

@enduml
